The translations just keep coming! Metabase is already available in [Spanish](/blog/metabase-in-spanish) and [Portuguese](/blog/metabase-in-portuguese), and with the release of [version 0.30.2](https://github.com/metabase/metabase/releases/tag/v0.30.2) we're happy to announce that French and Norwegian are available as well!

For the French translation, you can join us in thanking users Fabrice Etanchaud, Flegastelois, theniloc, Jean-Luc, Jtraulle, Corentin, Andrew Shaw, Antoine Brivazac, Christophe, Daniel Baldi, Delaunay.alexandre, Emmanuel, Helene, pmint93, Richard, Romain Ciaccafava, and Stéphane Boisson.

And for the Norwegian translation, we have Martin Madsen, Jostein Austvik Jacobsen, and Andreas Meyer Berntsen to thank.

To get Metabase in French or Norwegian (along with some bug fixes), [update to version 0.30.2](https://github.com/metabase/metabase/releases/tag/v0.30.2), and just set your browser’s preferred language to the language you'd like.

If you're interested in helping translate Metabase into a different language, you can [contribute here](https://poeditor.com/join/project/ynjQmwSsGh). Thanks in advance!

We'll keep updating you here as more languages become available, so stay tuned!
